{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For</b> — a lamed [prefix] added to the vow, like the third [psalm] for Absalom. The meaning: that I have vowed a vow, if You fulfill my request to dwell in Your tent." "And the meaning of <b>You have given the heritage</b> — that I may dwell in the land of Israel, which You gave as a heritage to those who fear Your name."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 61, :notes {0 "The third psalm's superscription לַאַבְשָׁלוֹם contains a prefixed lamed on a name; here too כִּי is read as an addition introducing a conditional vow."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:27.135783009Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}